course: dictionary
lesson: 1127
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Breast» is a good example. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «That cheerful robin is also one of the fiercest birds in the garden: its red breast is a warning flag.» Here a bird has a red breast, so breast means the front of its body. Ask yourself: what would fit in the sentence?
explain: Breast can also be a verb. To breast a hill means to reach its top by pushing forward with your chest. Some old stories and poems use breast for the heart, as in «hope in his breast».
fact: The breast is the front part of the chest of a person or animal.
fact: «Chicken breast» means the meat from the chest of a bird.
fact: In an old poem, «hope in his breast» means hope in his heart.
fact: «Robin redbreast» is a name for a robin, because of its red breast.
fact: «Make a clean breast of it» means to tell the whole truth and confess everything.
exercise: «Its red breast is a warning flag, and it will fight other robins.» In this sentence, what is the breast? | *The front of the bird's body, where the red feathers are | Its beak | Its wings | Its tail
exercise: «A chicken's legs are dark and its breast is pale.» Here breast means? | *The meat from the chest of a bird | A swimming style | The heart | To climb a hill
exercise: «The hiker had to breast the steep hill.» What does breast mean here? | To sing loudly | *To push forward and reach the top | To fall down | To cook slowly
test: What does «make a clean breast of it» mean? | To lose a game | To wash your shirt | *To confess everything | To run very fast
test: In the poem line «hope in his breast», what does breast mean? | His hand | His pocket | *His heart, the place of his feelings | His shoes
exam: «The American robin is a thrush, with a grey back and reddish breast.» In this sentence, breast means? | A swimming style | The top of a hill | A meat dish | *The front of the bird's body
